			"advancement": "lepidodendron:pf_adv_book_protosphyraena",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "Protosphyraena is a ray finned fish discovered in England dating back to most of the Creataceous. Its name is a mix of 'proto' and 'sphreana' which is the genus name for barracudas. This naming is due to the fact that it was thought to be a barracuda ancestor at first. Though with time and more research this is no longer the case. It was a relatively large animal, growing around 2 to 3 meters long."
		},
		{
			"advancement": "lepidodendron:pf_adv_book_protosphyraena",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "The genus was first discovered by Gideon Mantell in 1822, the man who discovered Iguanodon. Though it would not be named until 35 years later in 1857 by Joseph Leidy."
